---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import CertCard from '../components/CertCard.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="About - Tina Yan" description="About Tina Yan, UI/UX Designer. User research, UI design, and prototyping for user-centered digital experiences.">
  <Header currentPage="about" theme="editorial" />

  <main id="main-content" class="editorial about">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="editorial-grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="about-hero__inner max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-28 pb-16 lg:pt-32 lg:pb-20">
        <div class="about-hero__grid md:grid md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16 md:items-start items-center">
          <div class="about-hero__copy">
            <p class="editorial-eyebrow reveal" style="--i: 0">
              <span class="editorial-eyebrow__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              About · Toronto
            </p>
            <h1 class="about-hero__title reveal" style="--i: 1">
              Designer by <em class="about-hero__emphasis">choice</em>. Strategist by <em class="about-hero__emphasis">experience</em>.
            </h1>
            <div class="about-hero__body reveal" style="--i: 2">
              <p class="about-hero__lead">
                After years navigating complex stakeholder environments at TD, I made a deliberate move into UX. I design with both lenses: the user's and the business's.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="reveal" style="--i: 3">
              <a
                href={`${base}Resume_Tina-Yan.pdf`}
                download="Resume_Tina Yan.pdf"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="btn btn--primary"
                aria-label="Download Resume (opens in new window)"
              >
                Download resume
                <span class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="about-hero__portrait reveal" style="--i: 2">
            <div class="about-hero__frame">
              <img
                src={`${base}images/about-hero.png`}
                alt="Tina Yan"
                class="about-hero__img"
                width="600"
                height="600"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tabs: My Story / My Craft -->
    <section class="about-content" id="story">
      <div class="about-content__inner max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <header class="about-content__header reveal" style="--i: 0">
          <p class="editorial-eyebrow">Background</p>
          <div class="about-content__title-row">
            <h2 class="about-content__title">My story & craft</h2>
            <div class="about-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="About sections">
              <button
                type="button"
                role="tab"
                aria-selected="true"
                aria-controls="panel-story"
                id="tab-story"
                data-tab-button="story"
                class="about-tab is-active"
              >
                My Story
              </button>
              <button
                type="button"
                role="tab"
                aria-selected="false"
                aria-controls="panel-craft"
                id="tab-craft"
                data-tab-button="craft"
                class="about-tab"
              >
                My Craft
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Panel: My Story -->
        <div id="panel-story" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-story" data-tab-panel="story" class="about-panel">
          <div class="timeline">
            <div class="timeline__line" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="timeline-step timeline-step--reverse">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">The Pivot</h3>
                <p>I spent years watching people struggle with things that were built without them in mind. Confusing processes, unclear interfaces, workflows that created more friction. I wasn't a designer but I kept asking the same question: why is this so hard when it doesn't have to be?</p>
                <p>I wanted to be on the side that fixes it. Pivoting into UX was following a problem I couldn't stop noticing.</p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">Formalising the Craft</h3>
                <p>I formalised my design thinking through the Google UX Design Professional Certificate, but years at TD had already built the foundation.</p>
                <div class="cert-list">
                  <CertCard
                    title="Google UX Design Certificate"
                    issuer="Coursera"
                    issued="August 2025"
                    href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/specialization/X70EGDIDYX9F"
                    iconSrc={`${base}images/certs/500x500_Google.png`}
                  />
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step timeline-step--reverse">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">Learning in Motion</h3>
                <p>Transitioning while working full-time wasn't easy, studying courses, building prototypes, shipping designs. Time is running out, everything I have been through taught me how to keep moving without waiting for perfect conditions.</p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">Learning by Building</h3>
                <p>I learn by making: I try AI tools, build this portfolio in Cursor, use Claude and Figma MCP in my design process, and turn Anthropic's AI Fluency program into everyday practice.</p>
                <div class="cert-list">
                  <CertCard
                    title="AI Fluency: Framework & Foundations"
                    issuer="Anthropic"
                    issued="May 2026"
                    href="https://verify.skilljar.com/c/fbc3igddzgng"
                  />
                  <CertCard
                    title="Claude 101"
                    issuer="Anthropic"
                    issued="April 2026"
                    href="https://verify.skilljar.com/c/fcutpd2mg9a2"
                  />
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step timeline-step--reverse">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">How I Design</h3>
                <p>Research before assumptions. Clarity before polish. Always asking: does this make someone's life easier?</p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
              <article class="timeline-card">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">What I Bring to the Table</h3>
                <ul class="timeline-card__list">
                  <li><strong>Enterprise Literacy:</strong> Years at TD means I'm fluent in complexity, scale, and cross-functional collaboration. I understand how decisions get made, and I design with that reality in mind.</li>
                  <li><strong>Both Lenses:</strong> I don't just advocate for the user, I understand the business constraints behind every design decision.</li>
                  <li><strong>Clarity as a Craft:</strong> I specialise in stripping interfaces down to what actually matters. Clean, accessible, and purposeful without losing visual quality.</li>
                  <li><strong>Research-First Instinct:</strong> I ask why before I open Figma. Every decision is traceable back to a real user need or business objective.</li>
                </ul>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step timeline-step--reverse">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
              <article class="timeline-card">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">Key Skills</h3>
                <ul class="timeline-card__list">
                  <li><strong>Design & Tools:</strong> Figma, Wireframing, Prototyping, Design Systems, Accessibility (WCAG), Adobe Creative Suite, Miro</li>
                  <li><strong>AI & Workflow:</strong> Claude, Cursor, Figma MCP, Gemini, Maze, Claude 101 & AI Fluency certified (Anthropic)</li>
                  <li><strong>Process & Strategy:</strong> UX Research, Stakeholder Management, Cross-functional Collaboration, Design Thinking</li>
                </ul>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="timeline-step">
              <span class="timeline-step__num" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
              <article class="timeline-card timeline-card--narrative">
                <h3 class="timeline-card__title">Always Iterating</h3>
                <p>I'm building toward a version of myself that designs with more confidence, more craft, and more impact. I want to make things that genuinely change how someone's day feels. I'm curious, and I'm just getting started.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Panel: My Craft -->
        <div id="panel-craft" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-craft" data-tab-panel="craft" class="about-panel about-panel--craft hidden" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="craft-intro">
            <p class="craft-intro__quote">
              Beyond pixels and prototypes, my design philosophy is rooted in the tactile world.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="craft-gallery">
            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/coasters.jpg`} alt="Hand-painted ceramic coasters: landscapes, florals, and abstracts" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>A study in composition and texture beyond the screen. These hand-painted ceramic coasters explore color theory and tactile elements through varied themes like landscapes, florals, and abstracts.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/diptych.png`} alt="Diptych: circular form split across two canvases with gold metallic accents and blue gradients" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>
                <em>Painted from inspiration by another artist; source/author unknown.</em>
                A diptych exploring visual balance through high contrast and color gradients. By splitting a singular circular form across two canvases, I experiment with how focal points and metallic accents can unite disparate elements to create a cohesive, harmonious whole.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/forest.png`} alt="Stylized forest painting with metallic accents and cool blue palette, exploring depth and linear perspective" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>An exploration of depth and linear perspective through a stylized forest. By using varying scales and a central focal point, I created a sense of immersion. The metallic accents against the cool blue palette highlight my focus on creating visual interest through contrast.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/color-block-plant.png`} alt="Bold color blocking with minimalist plant illustration in yellow, teal, orange-red and black" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Bold color blocking meets minimalist illustration. This canvas highlights my focus on composition and spatial relationships, using a vibrant palette to create harmony between disparate shapes.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/photo-frame.png`} alt="Hand-painted photo frame with whimsical sky and daisy motif across outer and inner layers" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Exploring continuity by extending a whimsical sky and daisy motif across the layers of a photo frame. This piece demonstrates my eye for thematic consistency and my passion for transforming functional objects into engaging, delightful visual experiences that tell a story.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <h3 class="craft-section-title">Studies & Interpretations</h3>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/starry-night.png`} alt="Tribute to Van Gogh's The Starry Night with swirling sky and expressive brushwork" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>A tribute to Van Gogh's The Starry Night, exploring movement and rhythm through expressive brushwork. This piece demonstrates my eye for visual energy and flow, highlighting how swirling forms and high-contrast accents can guide a viewer's attention across a composition.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="craft-item">
              <img src={`${base}images/craft/water-lilies.png`} alt="Monet-inspired impressionist study of water lilies, willow branches, and serene light" width="4032" height="3024" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>An impressionist study of tranquility and light. Inspired by Monet, this painting explores organic forms and a serene palette, showcasing my eye for atmospheric harmony and my dedication to learning from classical masters to inform my modern design work.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script>
      const tabButtons = document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab-button]');
      const tabList = document.querySelector('[role="tablist"]');

      function activateTab(btn) {
        if (!btn) return;
        const tab = btn.getAttribute('data-tab-button');
        tabButtons.forEach((b) => {
          const selected = b === btn;
          b.setAttribute('aria-selected', selected ? 'true' : 'false');
          b.classList.toggle('is-active', selected);
        });
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab-panel]').forEach((panel) => {
          const show = panel.getAttribute('data-tab-panel') === tab;
          panel.classList.toggle('hidden', !show);
          panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', show ? 'false' : 'true');
        });
      }

      tabButtons.forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => activateTab(btn));
      });

      tabList?.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        const tabs = Array.from(tabButtons);
        const currentIndex = tabs.indexOf(document.activeElement);
        if (currentIndex === -1) return;
        let nextIndex = currentIndex;
        if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'ArrowDown') {
          e.preventDefault();
          nextIndex = (currentIndex + 1) % tabs.length;
        } else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'ArrowUp') {
          e.preventDefault();
          nextIndex = (currentIndex - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
        } else if (e.key === 'Home') {
          e.preventDefault();
          nextIndex = 0;
        } else if (e.key === 'End') {
          e.preventDefault();
          nextIndex = tabs.length - 1;
        }
        if (nextIndex !== currentIndex) {
          const next = tabs[nextIndex];
          if (next) {
            next.focus();
            activateTab(next);
          }
        }
      });
    </script>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <section id="contact" class="contact-section">
      <div class="contact-section__inner max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 reveal" style="--i: 0">
        <p class="contact-section__eyebrow">Collaborate</p>
        <h2 class="contact-section__title">Let's work together</h2>
        <p class="contact-section__desc">
          I'm open to full-time UX roles and design collaborations in Toronto and beyond. Let's make something worth using.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:yanlamji@gmail.com" class="btn btn--dark">
          yanlamji@gmail.com
          <span class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="site-footer__inner max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-6">
        <p class="site-footer__copy">@ Tina Yan 2026</p>
        <div class="site-footer__links">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tinayan-ysl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="site-footer__link" aria-label="LinkedIn (opens in new window)">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="mailto:yanlamji@gmail.com" class="site-footer__link" aria-label="Email Tina">Email</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ??About hero ??*/
  .about-hero {
    position: relative;
    min-height: min(90svh, 900px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--cream);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-hero::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: clamp(5rem, 14vw, 10rem);
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--paper-warm, #faf8f5));
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .about-hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 4.25rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 2.75rem;
  }

  .about-hero__emphasis {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .about-hero__lead {
    font-size: clamp(0.875rem, 1.25vw, 1rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .about-hero__portrait {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero__portrait {
      margin-top: 0;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: flex-end;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }

  .about-hero__frame {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 21rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.06);
    box-shadow:
      0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8) inset,
      0 16px 48px rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.1);
  }

  .about-hero__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* ??Content / tabs ??*/
  .about-content {
    --timeline-tail: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    padding: 4rem 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      var(--paper-warm, #faf8f5) 0%,
      var(--paper, #fff) 14%,
      var(--paper, #fff) 70%,
      var(--surface-blend, #f3f0ea) 100%
    );
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-content::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(246, 243, 238, 0.5), transparent);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .about-content__header {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
  }

  .about-content__title-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-content__title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-tabs {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 0.25rem;
    background: var(--cream);
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-left: auto;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--cream-deep);
  }

  .about-tab {
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .about-tab:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .about-tab.is-active {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.08);
  }

  .about-panel.hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ??Timeline ??*/
  .timeline {
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: var(--timeline-tail);
  }

  .timeline__line {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.25rem;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      var(--accent-soft),
      rgba(107, 166, 198, 0.35) 70%,
      rgba(235, 230, 220, 0.85) 100%
    );
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .timeline__line {
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
    }
  }

  .timeline-step {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-left: 3.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .timeline-step:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .timeline-step {
      padding-left: 0;
      width: 50%;
      margin-left: 0;
      padding-right: 2.5rem;
    }

    .timeline-step--reverse {
      margin-left: 50%;
      padding-right: 0;
      padding-left: 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  .timeline-step__num {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.15rem;
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--cream-deep);
    border-radius: 50%;
    z-index: 2;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.06);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .timeline-step__num {
      left: auto;
      right: -1.25rem;
    }

    .timeline-step--reverse .timeline-step__num {
      right: auto;
      left: -1.25rem;
    }
  }

  .timeline-card {
    flex: 1;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.06);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: 2.25rem 2.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.06);
    transition: box-shadow 0.25s ease;
  }

  .timeline-card:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.09);
  }

  .timeline-card--quote p {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .timeline-card__title {
    font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .timeline-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .timeline-card--narrative p {
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cert-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(20, 24, 32, 0.07);
  }

  .timeline-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .timeline-card__list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .timeline-card__list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .timeline-card__intro {
    margin-bottom: 1rem !important;
  }

  .timeline-card__tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .timeline-card__tags span {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* ??Craft gallery ??*/
  .about-panel--craft {
    --craft-gap: clamp(10rem, 20vw, 16rem);
    padding-top: max(0rem, calc(var(--craft-gap) - 6rem));
    padding-bottom: clamp(8rem, 18vw, 14rem);
  }

  .craft-intro {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin: 0 auto var(--craft-gap);
  }

  .craft-intro__quote {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
